			<div class="content" id="post-content-827705">
									

<p>@Yoric: Why does an addendum need to be clinical? I've seen plenty on this site which seemed much more like personal notes than formal additions to a formal document.</p>
<p>@SimpleCadence: Don't worry about it; your science nitpicking teaches me a little more about physics, and I figure the lesson is worth the edit. Do you have any idea how many thermal watts burning wood might release? (100&nbsp;kW/s is a wild guess).</p>
<p>Also, if you seal up the jar in concrete, you wouldn't be able to study it without cracking the concrete open. For the rest, I refer you to the second addendum and your imagination. Personally, I envision it somehow appearing outside of the container and tipping over. Or the container itself somehow splitting to accommodate the open jar. The scale-alarm system is more convenient than a lot of heavy-but-still-somehow-ineffective packaging and less expensive then trying to keep a fire burning inside a jar that constantly produces condensed water vapor.</p>

							</div>

								
					
